    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d485">

                <pb facs="0601" n="595" xml:id="pg595"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">711.6111/1: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The President of the Council of People’s Commissars of
                        the Soviet Union</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Stalin</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to President Roosevelt </hi><anchor n="69"
                        xml:id="d485-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Moscow</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1942-06-12">June 12, 1942</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>The Soviet Government shares your view, Mr. President, as to the satisfactory
                    results of Mr. V. M. Molotov’s visit to the United States.</p>
                <p>I take this opportunity to thank you, Mr. President, on behalf of the Soviet
                    Government, for the cordial hospitality offered to Mr. Molotov and his staff
                    during their sojourn in the United States.</p>
                <p>Mr. V. M. Molotov has safely returned to Moscow today.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d485-f1" n="69" type="source" xml:id="d485-f1-content">
                <p>This telegram was sent on June 13, 1942, by Ambassador Litvinov to Secretary of
                    State Hull for President Roosevelt, to whom it was transmitted on June 17.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
